# React Rules

- Prefer composition over prop drilling when components become too configurable.
- Do not put business logic into presentational components.
- Avoid unnecessary useEffect.
- Do not use useEffect for derived state if it can be calculated during render.
- Keep hooks focused on one responsibility.
- Custom hooks may orchestrate state, but UI packages must stay domain-agnostic.
- Memoization is allowed only when there is a clear reason.
- Do not add React.memo/useMemo/useCallback everywhere by default.